00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:13.490
Y-You mentioned that Tsukihi-chan stepped out,

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:14.620
but did Karen-san, too?

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:15.820
Yeah.

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:17.670
The two form one set.

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:18.940
It's a package deal.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:22.450
Wh-What about your parents?

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:25.760
My parents are out, or rather, they're working.

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:26.450
Working.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:35.250
Th-Then, I'm all alone with you today.

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:39.230
Well, now that you mention it, I guess we're alone.

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:40.550
Is something wrong with that?

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:42.940
Of course there's nothing wrong with it.

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:48.680
Then, for starters, welcome, Sengoku.

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:50.480
Y-Yeah!

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:53.140
I've been welcomed, Koyomi-oniichan!

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:54.290
Cheers!

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:56.520
Happy birthday!

00:03:57.860 --> 00:03:59.820
<i>My birthday is in April.</i>

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:06.200
<i>I finished telling Sengoku everything I needed to about the case with the con artist.</i>

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:08.500
Koyomi-oniichan.

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:14.070
Including my case, but, well, that con artist...

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:17.440
How in the world did he spread the rumors and stuff?

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:20.550
Rumors, or rather...

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:22.440
magic charms...

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:24.470
or maybe ghost stories?

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:25.970
That sort of stuff.

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:28.470
How? Of course...

00:04:30.070 --> 00:04:34.230
<i>Urban legends, idle rumors, secondhand information...</i>

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:41.150
<i>What specific methods are there to spread them
as the speaker rather than the listener?</i>

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:45.070
<i>How did that con artist spread the rumors?</i>

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:48.240
Who did they hear the rumor from in the first place?

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:50.920
From the con artist himself, right?

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:53.750
Everyone around me was saying,

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:57.380
it was "carried on the wind."

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:00.400
<i>The wind?</i>

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:07.660
The process of spreading a rumor.

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:10.860
The process of spreading a rumor, I guess.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:14.370
How did that con artist create such a gimmick?

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:21.770
If I was going to spread some sort of rumor,

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:23.670
I'd tell Tsukihi-chan first.

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:29.780
If I tell her, a celebrity and the face of middle school girls,

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:33.950
I think it'd be more effective than telling 100 people the same story.

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:39.790
Though I don't think the con artist
would contact high-profile people directly.

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:41.630
<b>I'M SURE HE PLANNED IT SO PEOPLE LIKE THAT</b>

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:41.630
<b>HEAR FROM A "FRIEND OF A FRIEND."</b>

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:45.710
I may be contradicting myself,

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:49.370
but I think, ideally, people would spread the rumor on their own,

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:52.660
without marketing efforts such as ads or commercials.

00:05:53.070 --> 00:05:57.290
But waiting for something to become popular on its own

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:59.630
is the same as it happening naturally.

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:02.330
Isn't that expecting a coincidence to occur?

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:11.320
<i>What you'd call an epilogue, or the punch line for this episode.</i>

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:12.330
A

