00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:12.330
14

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:15.730
The power to read the wind,

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:17.780
the power to create wind...

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:20.780
I don't have things of that nature.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:25.090
Though, even this statement may be a lie.

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:28.950
But, if you ask me,

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:31.880
the power to read wind isn't that important.

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:34.710
Because in a pandemic,

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:37.830
the most important thing is the lack of wind.

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:40.060
L-Lack of wind?

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:45.400
When something is a fad, nothing else can be a fad.

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:52.910
For example, I couldn't take action in this town during spring break.

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:57.870
Because the rumor of a "vampire" was the talk of the town.

00:06:57.870 --> 00:07:00.650
And after that rumor dissipated,

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:05.820
I fed a rumor into the now empty place,
a place that was now hungry for another.

00:07:06.170 --> 00:07:11.760
Ghost stories and wild rumors are prevalent
when human hearts are in a disarray.

00:07:12.210 --> 00:07:17.430
Human hearts being in disarray means there's nothing for them to believe in.

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:19.070
Araragi.

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:24.980
Think about the type of person a con artist would see as a sitting duck for his tricks.

00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:26.360
<b>I DON'T EVEN WANT TO THINK ABOUT IT.</b>

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:29.260
Obviously, it's the rich, right?

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:30.990
Wouldn't he go after the affluent?

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:32.110
<b>THAT'S WHAT A GOOD MAN WOULD THINK.</b>

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:35.910
Those who are fulfilled are surprisingly hard to deceive.

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:39.040
That's because humans with breathing room in their lives

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:41.830
have breathing room in their minds.

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:46.760
So, the con artist targets humans without breathing room in their lives,

00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:49.460
and who are unsatisfied with the status quo.

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:52.440
That's why, in this town,

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:54.590
you specifically targeted middle school girls?

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:57.340
Right.

00:07:57.880 --> 00:08:01.510
A heart filled with anxiety is easy to deceive.

00:08:01.510 --> 00:08:04.870
They don't have enough composure
to validate statements, even when lied to.

00:08:07.070 --> 00:08:09.540
You say I turned "magic charms" into a fad

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:14.820
that ruined interpersonal relationships as the base for my fraud.

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:17.700
But on that front, the truth is the opposite.

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:20.070
They jumped at my "magic charms"

00:08:20.070 --> 00:08:22.750
because their interpersonal relationships were already bad.

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:25.980
"It's only the fault of the duped," is what you want to say?

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:30.040
When you put it that way,
I don't want to say that anymore.

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:32.520
Let's just say it's bad times.

00:08:32.790 --> 00:08:38.410
If you want to discuss the chaotic situation,
like "Why the hell is something like this a fad?"

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:42.310
you ought to be discussing
the emptiness before the chaos.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:43.810
Emptiness?

00:08:43.810 --> 00:08:46.560
You can also call it the "darkness."

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:49.080
So, let me give you a warning.

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:52.090
If "something incomprehensible" shows up,

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:54.200
doubt the times you are in.

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:56.370
Feel that something is very wrong.

00:08:56.970 --> 00:09:01.600
Because it means that the times
are being enveloped by the "darkness."

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:05.100
Enveloped by the "darkness."

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:08.830
Now, Araragi.

00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:13.240
I just told you a precious, precious trade secret.

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:15.630
Of course, that requires an additional fee.

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:21.810
I know there's some rainy day money
stashed in the inner pocket of your jacket.

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:48.900
<b>Nayami ketobashite ishi ga korogatte ku</b>

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:48.900
<b>Kicking a stone as if I was kicking my troubles</b>

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:54.650
<b>Sukoshi gomakashita are wa shigatsu no koto</b>

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:54.650
<b>It was April when I played my trick</b>

00:09:54.860 --> 00:10:00.120
<b>Koukishin ousei de akarui kodomo deshita</b>

00:09:54.860 --> 00:10:00.120
<b>I was a curious and cheerful child</b>

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:05.870
<b>Senaka oshita no wa ano hi kara no boku de</b>

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:05.870
<b>The me from the past gave me a push</b>

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:11.750
<b>Hamidasenai retsu wo oinuite</b>

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:11.750
<b>Let's loiter on the way</b>

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:17.340
<b>Michikusa wo shiyou</b>

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:17.340
<b>Passing a line you can't even lean out from</b>

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:25.020
<b>Kago ni nose taisetsu na yume</b>

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:25.020
<b>I'll put my precious dreams in the basket</b>

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:30.400
<b>pedaru mawashi tooku made saa mochi dasou</b>

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:30.400
<b>and spin the pedals, carrying them far away!</b>

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:35.780
<b>Uwasa shita boku no mirai wa</b>

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:35.780
<b>My rumored future...</b>

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:37.550
<b>Kokochi iino?</b>

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:37.550
<b>Am I comfortable with it?</b>

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:40.860
<b>Nobiru kage ni kiitemo</b>

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:40.860
<b>I even asked my long shadow;</b>

00:10:41.110 --> 00:10:49.710
<b>Wakaranai wakaranai wakaranai</b>

00:10:41.110 --> 00:10:43.910
<b>It doesn't know a thing...</b>

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:46.660
<b>It doesn't know a thing...</b>

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:49.710
<b>It doesn't know a thing...</b>
